METHODS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Item 3a — Study Design:
✅ REPORTED: Cross-sectional observational quantitative survey design.

Item 3b — Setting & Dates:
✅ REPORTED: Conducted in Syria between 10 March and 15 April 2026 via structured electronic data collection across faculties, syndicate channels, and manufacturing sites.

Item 3c — Eligibility Criteria:
✅ REPORTED: Pharmacy degree holders or active pharmacy students in Syria; exclusion of non-pharmacy backgrounds, duplicates, and >50% missing data.

Item 4 — Variables & Operationalization:
✅ REPORTED: Formative Composite Indices (PILS, IAI, IRS, IPI, Diagnostic Gap) defined with item counts, normalization (0–100), and floor effect metrics.

Item 5 — Measurement & Data Sources:
✅ REPORTED: Google Forms electronic survey platform with single-response enforcement. Formative measurement philosophy explicitly justified.

Item 6a — Bias Control:
⚠️ PARTIALLY REPORTED: Single-response technical enforcement; convenience sampling acknowledged as limitation in Section 4.4.

Item 6b — Study Size:
✅ REPORTED: Target 400 distributed invitations; 303 verified complete responses (75.83% response rate).

Item 7 — Quantitative Variables:
✅ REPORTED: Descriptive distributions reported with Mean, SD, Median, IQR, Skewness, and Zero-count/percentage.

Item 8 — Statistical Methods:
✅ REPORTED: Spearman rank correlation, One-way ANOVA, Kruskal-Wallis, Multivariable Tobit MLE regression (left-censored at 0), Binary Logistic regression, LOWESS curve estimation.

